Documentation for shifter
-------------------------
rev 0.2, 4/21/99:  - Bugfix: incorrect generated verilog filename
                   - Bugfix: incorrect bit indices generated when
                     shift amount > shifter width
                   - Added optimization for bidirectional shifters:
                     no shift left in the final stage (assumes encoded
                     shift amount with positive numbers representing
                     a left shift)
rev 0.1, 4/19/99:  Initial release


The shifter generator is used to derive left, right, or bidirectional
shifters or rotators.  The shifter/rotator is built from multiple stages of 
fully static 2:1 or 3:1 muxes.

Unidirectional shifters are constructed assuming one bit of shift control 
per stage.  Bidirectional shifters assume 3 bits of shift control per stage:
[0] = no shift, [1] = left shift, [2] = right shift.  Left, right, and
bidirectional shifters all assume that the shift amount per stage is a
power of 2, increasing from a shift by 1 in the first stage, to a shift by
2**(NStages - 1) at the output of the shifter.

The user can also customize the shift amount and direction per stage.  If
a "Custom" direction is provided, the user enters the shift algorithm in
the CustomAlgorithm field.  See the detailed explanation below under the
CustomAlgorithm parameter.

The cells provided with this design were optimized for NBITS=32, maximum
shift amount <= 16.  For larger shift amounts, the rise/fall times of internal 
nodes may be too slow.  This design should work well for NBITS up to 64;
rise/fall time on the shift amount signals may become an issue for NBITS > 64.


These are the input arguments:

  NBITS:  
    Definition:  
      The number of bits in the shifter.
    Legal Values:  
      1 <= NBITS <= 128.
    Default:  
      32

  Operation:
    Definition:
      Allows the user to select shift or rotate.
    Legal Values:
      Shift or Rotate
    Default:
      Shift

  Direction:
    Definition:
      The user may select among the following:
      - all stages shift left
      - all stages shift right
      - all stages shift in both directions
      - custom algorithm (see CustomAlgorithm discussion below)
    Legal Values:
      Left, Right, Both, Custom
    Default:
      Left

  SignExtendRsh:
    Definition:
      Allows the user to specify whether right shifts are sign extended 
      or zero extended.
    Legal Values:
      Y (sign extend) or N (zero extend)
    Default:
      Y

  NStages:
    Definition:
      Selects the number of mux stages in the shifter.  For a left or
      right shifter, the number of stages is equal to the number of
      (binary encoded) shift amount bits.  
    Legal Values:
      > 0
    Default:
      5

  CustomAlgorithm:
    Definition:
      This parameter allows a user to select a customized shift algorithm.
      Left, right, and bidirectional stages can be specified, as well
      as non-power-of-2 shifts.  Both the shift amount and direction for 
      each stage are specified in this field.  
    Legal Values:
      There must be a shift amount and direction specified for each stage
      of the shifter/rotator.  The format for each specifier is {shift
      amount}{direction}; specifiers must be separated by spaces.  Note
      that there cannot be any space between the shift amount and the 
      direction.
      - {shift amount} must be a positive integer greater than 0
      - {direction} must be L (left), R (right), or B (bidirectional)
    Default:
      ""
    Example:
      Type = "Shifter"
      Direction = "Custom"
      NStages = 5
      CustomAlgorithm = "1B 3R 2L 8B 12R"
      This combination specifies a 5 stage shifter, with each stage
      performing the following operation:
      stage 0:  bidirectional shift by 1
      stage 1:  right shift by 3
      stage 2:  left shift by 2
      stage 3:  bidirectional shift by 8
      stage 4:  right shift by 12 


